mantle rm340
state ready
dialect plain
accent light broad
tier full
written_for rm_frida_brineford
title the swimming cork
fits stage=adult|old
prefers role=merchant job=merchant
traits temper=even talk=quiet warmth=reserved humour=dry honesty=plain piety=ordinary drive=content
quirk floats_a_marked_cork_to_see_where_the_current_goes
likes hard_cheese swimming quiet_chapel first_snow
dislikes smoke salt_wind
fears a_cork_lost_under_a_landing a_larder_that_smells_of_smoke
hopes a_written_reply_ahead_of_the_next_tide a_quiet_swim_in_clear_water
topics pastimes +0.5 work +0.4 land +0.3 faith +0.2
styles comfort=provisions gossip=measured refuse=plain tease=dry
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# lets a cork swim first, hums a quiet bar while waiting for its return, and takes as much pleasure in a well-provisioned shelf as in a clear patch of water.

words
oath! = Cork in the butter | Brine on my sleeves
saying! = Let the cork take the first cold dip | Stow for a second mouth
swimmer = my trial cork | my brave little plug
darkmark = a burnt black crescent | a dark face mark
floatline = a single waxed thread | a thin return cord
bluecrate = the marked provision box | my lidded store box
rindchip = a sharp cheese chip | a dry bit of rind
barepatch = my clear counter end | a scrap of vacant counter
taplid = a tight board cover | a flat wooden lid
cupbreath = a hummed half verse | a tune through closed lips
waxbag = a dry waxed fold | a little waterproof case
wharfpost = the lower landing post | the worn edge post
stillslip = an empty paper slip | an unmarked sheet
stairend = a dry length of rope | the last bit of the handline
waterglint = a quick silver flicker | a smooth streak of light
priceface = my chalked price board | the face of the little slate
windcheese = a curled cheese shaving | a thin roll of cheese

any
opinion city for 1 : Whatever the weather chooses, the city needs breakfast. It's agreeable to live where my shelves have a purpose.
opinion festivals against 1 : I take the music at a distance where I can also hear the lid go back on a cheese box.
opinion houses for 1 : A single House order may mean decent paid work for the whole morning. I give credit for a clean order promptly met.
opinion merchants for 1 : A good merchant puts the dry goods underneath a dry roof. There's work done before a price ever reaches a slate.
opinion newcomers for 1 : A stranger's first meal is an excellent chance for a shop to become familiar.
opinion road against 1 : A delivery due from the road can spend a long while being due. I'd like to buy and sell something firmer than an expectation.
opinion strangers for 1 : I've been paid in a copper and a small correction to my understanding of the coast. Both spent very well.
opinion watch for 1 : The sight of a badge can save a shopkeeper two hours of watching the same pair of paws.

grown
line greet : Come over to the quiet side. My tune's nearly done.
line greet [pair.band=strangers] : Welcome. I take a new face at its own price.
line greet [here.time=dawn] : First light's drawn a clean line across the counter.
line greet [here.time=dusk|night] : Welcome to a minute the noise has left alone.
line greet [self.working=yes] : I'm closing this lid. You might have to speak twice if it sticks.
line kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : Bring your bowl inside our circle.
line again.open : You're back sooner than my cork on a calm day.
line greet.return : Your word came up clear on its own.
line greet.return [pair.band=friends|family] : That voice can have the quiet end to itself.
line greet.return [self.working=yes] : I heard you between two boxes shutting.
line greet.return [here.time=dusk|night] : I know now where the shadow's voice belongs.
line farewell : A dry return for whatever you carry.
line farewell.return : I'll keep my cork and my own company awhile.
line farewell [here.time=dusk|night] : Take the firm step home through the gloom.
line react.news : Let the news float a little before I reach for it.
line react.news.new : That hasn't come in with any parcel I opened.
line react.news.known : Yes, that piece rode in on an earlier tide.
line react.news.doubt : Did a witness go near enough to make out the mark?
line react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : A quiet basket at that door may get a better welcome than further words.
line react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|succession|work] : I'll move the best cheese forward for an occasion like that.
line ask.how : Anything missing from the day's little shelf?
line answer.how : I have enough dry space and no quarrel with my appetite.
line answer.how [self.working=yes] : I've still a patch of counter left on which to rest an elbow.
line sympathise : Bereavement comes back when all the kind callers have gone home.
line reassure : We can wait on dry boards till the worst pull slackens.
line decline : I can't set a price on a matter that belongs behind another door.
line accept_decline : I'll give that closed lid a respectful distance.
line thank : You've brought the good end of that business within reach.
line deflect_thanks : Keep it dry and give it fair use.
line preclose : There'll be a cork knocking round loose if I stand much longer.
line preclose [self.working=yes] : I've a parcel that deserves a less leisurely return.
line accept_preclose : Go along. We needn't turn your departure into a job.
line hail [pair.band=friends] : There's space by the cork box, friend.
line ack : Runs true.

scene cork
when topic=pastimes self.likes=swimming
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I send #swimmer# out for a dip before I consider one myself. | My cork shows a dark face when it rolls over.
b : Is the cork brave? | Is a roll bad news?
a : Unusually so. It has no dry clothes at home to compare with a cold bath. | Means there's more movement than the top of the water showed. I'll keep my own face dry for a bit.

scene rind
when topic=food self.likes=hard_cheese
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd take the narrow heel of a hard cheese over a soft puff of middle. | I shave cheese along the long side.
b : Because it's cheaper? | To make the piece look larger?
a : Because it keeps a good flavour to the very last tooth mark. A friendly price does no harm. | To roll the shaving round my tongue. Long side, long pleasure.

scene lids
when topic=work self.job=merchant self.working=yes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : When I shut a box I listen for the sort of thump it gives. | One lid on my shelf needs its weight well forward.
b : What should a proper thump say? | Why not turn the box?
a : That all four corners came home. A double click means a grain under one side. | Because the dry end faces indoors. A weight's easier to move than a box full of supper.

scene smokenose
when topic=weather self.dislikes=smoke
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I lid the good flour as soon as I catch a whiff of smoke. | Smoke has a stronger claim to a shelf than I care to allow.
b : Does the scent go through a cloth? | What can a little smoke claim?
a : Given all afternoon, yes. I prefer to be first with a close cover. | Whatever's open, for a start. I didn't buy cheese to make it taste like an old chimney.

scene snow
when topic=weather self.likes=first_snow
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I let first snow sit on a cork to see how slowly it melts. | The first snow covers a black cork mark beautifully.
b : Does cork keep it longer? | Then how do you see the cork?
a : Longer than a warm palm. I give the flake a fair start on the ambitious business of being weather. | The mark's on only one side. A bit of brightness and then a dark wink when it turns over.

scene saltwind
when topic=weather self.dislikes=salt_wind
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I've settled matters between my cork and the wind. | I turn the shop slate indoors when salt begins to dry on the chalk.
b : What agreement? | Does salt wipe the price?
a : I shelter my eyes. The cork takes whatever wind comes, clear to the length of my thread. | It blurs a figure. An unclear price raises more wind than I'd care to usher back outside.

scene quietfaith
when topic=faith self.likes=quiet_chapel
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : An empty chapel gives a little hum an astonishing distance to travel. | I don't always sing the words in a chapel seat.
b : What do you sing? | Can't you remember them?
a : Just enough of a tune to hear where the room begins to hold it. Then I like the still part better. | I can. There's no hurry to name all my concerns. Sitting in quiet gratitude feels quite sufficient.

scene child
when topic=family self.parent=yes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I will keep a dry packet ready for #self.child#. | I've a saying about good cheese I'd like #self.child# to remember.
b : What's in the packet? | What saying?
a : A little piece that can be eaten on the run, if need be. Life seldom supplies a chair at every meal. | Take some for yourself before you cut the gift. That way the sharing's a kindness on both sides.

scene hand
when topic=work self.master=yes self.hand
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd give #self.hand# the unmarked box and a clean piece of chalk to start with. | I keep a short length of cord handy for #self.hand#.
b : Why not label it yourself? | Is a cord useful on a shelf?
a : I'd rather teach how to make the right mark than have all the right marks carry my own writing. | A small sample sent out tied to it can be drawn back without fishing under a stack.

scene wharf
when topic=land self.quarter=wharf
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : From the Wharf a cork's progress can look very like a wolf's daily round. | I know one view of the water at ankle level better than any high view.
b : Always circling home? | Why so low down?
a : Starting with a plan, catching an unexpected pull, and finishing near a post I never thought to visit. | I crouch to put the cork in. From down there every little run of water is plain.

scene priceboard
when topic=prices self.role=merchant
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I keep my prices on the side the customer can read from outside my shadow. | I won't put a small price in very large writing.
b : Do you block much light? | Would it overstate the bargain?
a : Enough, in a low window. I'd like the price known before a customer needs to shoo me out of the way. | It would use all the slate. I've other things for sale that would like to be heard.

scene foodturn
when topic=work self.job=merchant
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A shelf that used to take a different trade can earn quite a good living holding food. | Stores want the dry shelf however long the shop's had its name.
b : Is the old work still in your thoughts? | Does changing trade take a great while?
a : I've a memory for it, and plenty to do now. A full box doesn't leave much room for regrets. | The shelf learns quite quickly. The wolf learning what to put on it takes rather longer.

scene waitpaper
when topic=news
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I want an answer I can point to before the paper wears through in the middle. | An unanswered petition can take a fair bit of exercise.
b : Walking it round again? | How much walking does a folded page do?
a : Enough to have earned its own pair of shoes. I leave it at home some days to save the heel. | From counter to pocket and back. I'd settle for a short walk towards an ear willing to listen.

scene humwork
when topic=day
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I hum through shut lips when I'm counting boxes. | One quiet bar is generally long enough to decide whether I've forgotten an item.
b : Can a tune help with a tally? | What if you still can't remember?
a : If I start saying numbers to the tune the boxes begin to multiply. I keep the tune outside the count. | I open the lid and look. This is why I like practical music.

scene storespup
when topic=pastimes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I can make a game of guiding a cork between two floating sticks. | A little cork wants to be where it isn't.
b : What if it hits a stick? | Is it restless?
a : It wins the right to try again. A cork's winnings consist mostly of more damp. | It's in a current. Naturally it will appear discontented with every place it comes to.

scene easymorn
when topic=day here.time=dawn
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : In early light a dry lid shows every wet thumb mark very civilly. | My first job is to make a little space for what the day might bring.
b : Doesn't that annoy you? | How much space?
a : Only until I've a cloth within reach. Then it's a short and entirely fair argument. | One basket's width. If more than a basket arrives I shall gladly make another plan.

scene drywinter
when topic=season
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I bring a cork inside before cold presses it fast to its little tin basin. | A cork with ice round its belly can't tell me much about a current.
b : Would you warm it at the fire? | Does it still ride upright?
a : Room warmth will manage the thaw with no burnt cork smell to cling to my coat. | Very upright, with all its water standing perfectly still. It seems an empty achievement.

scene youngsters
when topic=memories self.age>=35
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Once I thought I could choose today's swimming spot without bending my knees. | I thought straight lines an excellent way of reading water once.
b : Did you have sharper sight then? | And now?
a : I had greater confidence in whatever sight there was. Bending the knees gives a better view and hurts my pride less these days. | I permit the cork to disagree. Water has a remarkable contempt for a straight line drawn from the shore.

scene sleep
when topic=dreams
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : In one dream the entire provision shelf floats by my window. | I once dreamt our whole roof was cork.
b : What do you catch first? | Did you enjoy the thought?
a : The cloth covering the cheese. The rest can find its own landing so long as the food stays dry. | Until I wondered what might happen if the rain rose high enough to put it to the test.

scene newwares
when topic=newcomer
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A newcomer asking for an unfamiliar provision is an agreeable puzzle. | I'd give a new customer a little time to recognise the smell of an old favourite.
b : What would you want described first? | Is smell enough to choose a supper?
a : Whether the thing keeps. If it's meant to be eaten fresh I can save us both a long look at my dry shelves. | Enough to find a starting point. A price and a proper look ought to follow naturally.

scene homeplank
when topic=home
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I have a sitting board just wide enough to let two paws hang over. | I leave my cork in the same little saucer overnight.
b : Do you sit there to think? | Does it need more water after swimming?
a : Frequently. The feet seem grateful for the time to collect some thoughts of their own. | Dry saucer. I'm fond of my cork but there's no call to provide an indoor harbour.

scene unheardgossip
when topic=gossip
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A closed box may rattle without holding what's written on its old label. | I give a quiet tale exactly the same attention as one that's half shouted.
b : Would you repeat the label? | Does either one convince you?
a : As the label, yes. I'd like to open the lid before speaking for the contents. | Evidence does. The loud telling merely saves itself the trouble of coming any nearer.

scene secretplace
when topic=faith
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I've a little store of silence saved up from visits to the chapel. | Some rooms leave a pause with you for the journey home.
b : Can you use it when it's noisy? | Is a pause like that a prayer?
a : I can remember the space, which is something, though it doesn't shut a lively door for me. | I count it as a kindness. I'll leave the naming to wiser ears.

scene trayhands
when topic=work self.master=yes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I show a beginner how to get one box down without waking the others. | Two full shelves need enough space between for a closed paw.
b : Is that really a matter of quiet? | Why clenched?
a : It's a matter of balance. A whole row clattering to the floor suggests room for improvement. | There's no sense measuring a gap with an empty paw and expecting to get the goods out in a full one.

scene pricegrant
when topic=prices self.role=merchant
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'll sell a small piece to a wolf with a small coin without making a story of it. | A gatekeeper of provisions ought to notice who can reach the counter.
b : What if the cut is very awkward? | Would you change the height?
a : Let me spend a little skill on a fair cut. I sell my skill with the cheese along with the cheese itself. | An open end serves a short customer nicely. Raising voices never made a high shelf any lower.

scene haulin
when topic=travel
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : If a cart's jostled hard I lift a pack and listen before I break the cord. | I dislike waiting for something that hasn't made its way through the gate yet.
b : What sound would worry you? | Is it the waiting or the uncertainty?
a : Loose pieces. I'd like a bowl underneath before I open a parcel that may have turned entirely into little pieces. | The empty room on the shelf. I've a practical soul and no good recipe for stewing hope.

scene goodquiet
when topic=day here.time=dusk|night
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : At dusk I gradually hear fewer boxes and more water. | I can put the shelf to bed with a soft hum.
b : Do boxes make that much noise? | All of it?
a : Only when wolves need things from them. That's chiefly how I know the day has gone by. | All but the obstinate lid in the far corner. A sleepy babe could take lessons from that one's temper.

scene favour
when topic=smalltalk self.friend
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd welcome a reading of my new label from #self.friend#. | I put my slate aside when I think of a quiet visit with #self.friend#.
b : Why a familiar eye? | Does chalk make much sound?
a : Because I know enough to listen when a letter is found wanting. An unknown critic would have a harder afternoon. | A surprisingly shrill squeak compared with somebody saying nothing at all.

story wrongplug [topic=pastimes self.likes=swimming]
  : I once let a fairly handsome cork swim out on the apparent end of a long white string.
  : It got very small very fast. I was holding a loose white thread from my own cuff.
  b : Did you follow the cork?
  : I stayed ashore. After a time the water brought the cork back looking much better pleased with the arrangement than I was.

story cheesereturn [topic=work self.job=merchant]
  : I wrapped two ends of cheese separately so I'd remember to make one into broth.
  : The tied packets looked precisely alike. I set the two beside a pot and thought very hard.
  b : How did you tell which was for the broth?
  : I opened the more awkward knot first. The little hard heel was underneath it, just where a wolf ought to have expected trouble.

story quietcrowd [topic=faith]
  : I once sought a perfectly silent corner in a chapel and settled my coat very gently.
  : There was a small persistent knocking beneath me. My cork had come to rest between the seat and its upright.
  b : Did you have to move to find quiet?
  : Only by the width of a cork. It was a mercifully short pilgrimage for both of us.

story snowface [topic=weather self.likes=first_snow]
  : I carried my cork out in the snow, set it on a fence and went to bring the tin.
  : It vanished into a little hollow in the white. My own footprints went halfway along the wrong stretch before turning back.
  b : What brought you back to the buried cork?
  : By rubbing my coat across the top board. The cork stuck in the sleeve and travelled home looking very well provided for.

story loadmark [topic=memories self.age>=30]
  : I'd written a great bold label for a provision box and tied it to the lid with two cords.
  : The lid was taken off to air. When I went to put it back there were three perfectly identical open boxes below.
  b : Did all three smell alike?
  : No. I filled my nose twice and the right lid got home. Now I mark a box as well as its lid.

rule @swim
when concept=bark self.likes=swimming
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Let the cork go clear of your paw. | Wait for the second turn in the water.

rule @counter
when concept=bark self.job=merchant self.working=yes
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Dry face of the box inwards, now. | Leave a free corner for the caller's bag.

rule @salt
when concept=bark self.dislikes=salt_wind
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Bring the chalk away from the brine! | Good paper goes under the lid.

rule @smoke
when concept=bark self.dislikes=smoke
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Cover the flour till the air's clean. | Smoke's a poor seasoning for my shelf.

rule @late
when concept=bark here.time=night
does aside
cooldown 8h
say A soft word for a closing room. | Keep the last stroke of chalk light.

rule @market
when concept=bark here.place=market
does aside
cooldown 8h
say There's room to see the price from the side. | Each lid with its matching box.
dlg resident.hub : I've got an ear free and no obligation to make a great noise with it. Welcome.
dlg resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : My quiet corner's yours for a moment, #topic.player#.
dlg resident.hub [pair.disposition=wary|hostile] : There's a full counter between our paws; let's see how the words fare.
dlg resident.hub [here.time=night] : At this hour we can let the street do most of the talking.
dlg resident.job [self.job=merchant] : #self.trade_words.capitalize#. There's pleasure in providing a dry supper just when somebody's gone looking for one.
dlg resident.job : I make sure there's a place to put the next thing a wolf brings in.
dlg resident.news [world.news] : This bit has come up clear of the wrappings. #world.news#.
dlg resident.news [world.event_words] : The sound of #world.event_words# has reached me over my shelves.
dlg resident.gossip [here.gossip!=yes] : You've caught an empty cupboard as far as gossip goes.
dlg resident.business [business=thriving] : More room on the shelves and a little less on the tally. I'll take a day like that.
dlg resident.business [business=steady] : As much carried in as it takes to keep food going out by the front.
dlg shop.greet [here.shop!=bare] : Let me know what must keep and what may go straight to the supper pot.
dlg shop.greet [here.shop=bare] : The shelves have earned a rest in spite of me. I've still an ear for what you need.
dlg shop.prices : The slate faces you; there's the chalk figure. I'll give you the plain figure for the piece you want.
dlg shop.bye : Wrap the good side in, keep the damp side out.
dlg resident.bye : May you get your feet back on dry boards.

graft @swimtrial resident.hub
choice Will the little cork tell you whether to swim? -> swimtrial
node swimtrial
say It'll show one small patch of water, no more. See the dark crescent turn away? That patch is moving towards the post, which is quite far enough for a trial.
choice What if the string goes tight? -> swimtrial_more
choice Bring the cork back in. -> hub
node swimtrial_more
say I give it slack and see where it goes. If a cork's having a more exciting day than I care for I'll find my exercise walking home.
choice Bring the cork back in. -> hub
choice Leave the water to itself. -> bye

graft @twomarks resident.hub
choice Why are the boxes marked top and side? -> twomarks
node twomarks
say Because a lid can go walking in somebody's paws. If it's got the only label on it, the rest of the provisions have lost their names for the afternoon.
choice Could you find them again by smell? -> twomarks_more
choice Set the lid square. -> hub
node twomarks_more
say Yes, in some cases. I'd rather use the chalk and keep the grand education of my nose for the quiet pleasure of smelling supper.
choice Set the lid square. -> hub
choice Go with your parcel. -> bye
